From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 02:56:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Added: Change the terminal font size with A+ and A- extra
 keys

The default extra keys have A+ right of PGUP and A- right of PGDN, which
make the terminal text larger or smaller on the screen. Like pinch zoom
and Ctrl+Alt+/-, which now do the same, the size is not saved, so the
saved size is used when the app is opened again.

The saved size is set in a new Font size dialog, from the Size button
of the Font dialog or Settings > Terminal View > Font size, with a
sample of the text at that size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GLNsTPnn2xKUQ4uFcevT6G
